{"chunk_id": "4a917583d684", "text": "After Ravana\u2019s fall, the battlefield erupts in cosmic celebration. The monkey hosts shout in triumph while the gods beat celestial drums and shower Rama\u2019s chariot with flowers from the sky, proclaiming his victory and the end of the terror that oppressed the worlds. Peace seems to return to nature itself: winds soften, the earth steadies, and the sun shines clearly again. Rama\u2019s allies\u2014Sugriva, Vibhishana, Angada, and Lakshmana\u2014approach the victorious hero. Yet joy is tempered by grief when Vibhishana sees his brother Ravana lying dead. He delivers a powerful lament, recalling Ravana\u2019s former glory through grand metaphors of tree, elephant, fire, and bull. Rama answers with sober warrior wisdom, insisting Ravana did not fall through weakness and that those who die bravely in battle should not be mourned, urging Vibhishana to perform his duty.\nAfter Ravana\u2019s death, Vibhishana mourns his fallen brother with vivid metaphors, while Rama counsels that a warrior slain in battle should not be lamented.\nThemes: brotherly grief, warrior dharma, aftermath of victory, honor in battle, moral reflection", "vector": [-0.00853746198117733, -0.028794046491384506, 0.008245809003710747, 0.001174895209260285, -0.0037848528008908033, 0.01191134937107563, -0.017446117475628853, -0.018745295703411102, -0.027110418304800987, -0.006833946332335472, 0.0020581381395459175, 0.006820689421147108, 0.007821587845683098, 0.0036058842670172453, 0.002671270864084363, 0.01181855145841837, 0.049262743443250656, -0.014569363556802273, 0.03666866198182106, -0.018016165122389793, 0.006035216618329287, 0.005229858215898275, -0.020070988684892654, -0.004643239080905914, -0.02115805633366108, 0.017963137477636337, 0.02294774167239666, -0.024869997054338455, 0.023226138204336166, 0.0037583389785140753, -0.003513085888698697, -0.008915283717215061, -0.004268730990588665, 0.0023680187296122313, -0.018891122192144394, -0.004010220523923